   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Look, this is a leather belt.' Notice the word order: 'look' comes first, and 'belt' finishes the sentence. Then Senya replies.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Зачем он тебе на кухне?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why do you have it in the kitchen?' The key word here means 'what for', which Senya combines with 'he'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я буду его есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am going to eat it.' The first content word means 'I', and 'there is' rounds out the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Это кожаный ремень?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Is it a leather belt?' Senya starts with 'this' and pairs it with 'leather' to make the point clear.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Он очень длинный.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It is very long.' The key word here means 'he', which Senya combines with 'very much'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я повар.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am a chef.' Fedya starts with 'I' and pairs it with 'chef' to make the point clear.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я приготовлю и съем.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will cook it and eat it.' Fedya puts 'I' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'will prepare'. Senya answers straight away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Никто не ест ремни.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nobody eats belts.' In Russian, 'nobody' leads into 'belt' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А я буду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'But I will.' Here 'I' sets up the idea, while 'will be' comes at the end for emphasis.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Хорошо, готовь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'All right, cook it.' You'll hear 'good' all the time in the show, here connected with 'prepare'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я посмотрю на это.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will watch this.' Notice the word order: 'I' comes first, and 'this' finishes the sentence.",
